@startuml secure-login-flow
' Sample PUML for parser tests — hardened against the STRIDE findings from the backend.
title Sample Login Flow (STRIDE-Hardened)
skinparam shadowing false

actor "End User" as user
participant "CDN + WAF" as waf
participant "Web App" as web
boundary "Auth Gateway" as authgw
control     "Auth Service"   as auth
entity      "Secret Manager" as vault
participant "DB Firewall"    as dbfw
database    "User DB"        as udb
queue       "Audit Queue"    as q
participant "SIEM"           as siem

user   -->  waf    : HTTPS request
waf    -->  web    : forward over TLS
web    -->  web    : input validation
web    --> authgw : credentials (mTLS)
authgw ->  auth   : validate
auth   ->  vault  : fetch signing keys
auth   ->  dbfw   : query user
dbfw   -->  udb    : authorized SELECT
udb    --> dbfw   : profile
dbfw   --> auth   : profile
auth   --> q      : signed audit event
q      --> siem   : ship logs
auth   --> web    : generic reject on invalid

note right of waf
  Mitigates S (waf):
  validates and sanitizes all headers,
  IP allowlist for backend access,
  strict TLS with certificate pinning.
end note

note right of web
  Mitigates R (web):
  comprehensive audit logging of all user
  actions and authentication attempts,
  ships logs to SIEM with full forensic
  context (user, IP, UA, request id).
end note

note right of auth
  Mitigates E (auth):
  short-lived JWTs (5-15 min) with refresh,
  automated key rotation,
  anomaly detection on token usage,
  least-privilege Secret Manager access.
end note

note right of vault
  Mitigates I (vault):
  HSM-backed key storage,
  least-privilege access policy,
  audit log on every key access,
  key versioning with automatic rotation.
end note

note right of dbfw
  Mitigates I (dbfw):
  parameterized queries only,
  least-privilege DB account,
  output validation before returning rows,
  monitoring for unusual query patterns.
end note

note right of udb
  Mitigates T (udb):
  database audit logging on all writes,
  row-level security policies,
  database activity monitoring (DAM),
  every modification traceable to a user.
end note

note right of q
  Mitigates D (q):
  rate limit on event ingestion,
  bounded queue size with overflow policy,
  backlog metrics + alerting,
  dead-letter queue for spillover.
end note

note right of siem
  Mitigates T (siem):
  append-only immutable storage (WORM),
  cryptographic signing for log integrity,
  strict access controls,
  alerting on unauthorized access attempts.
end note

@enduml
